# Branch: hold for main (until next month)

Until the user explicitly says to merge / push this work to **main**:

- **Active branch:** `wip/next-month-main`
- Put **all** new commits on this branch (checkout it first if needed).
- **While iterating:** after meaningful chunks of work, **commit and push this branch** (`git push -u origin HEAD`) so WIP is on the remote — do **not** wait for an explicit “push” each time (unless the user said not to). Same habit as `feature-branch-wip-push.mdc`.
- When the user asks to **push** (without saying main): push **only** this branch.
- **Do not merge into `main`**, create a main-bound release, or `git push origin main` unless the user clearly asks (e.g. "merge to main", "push to main").
- Prefer rebasing this branch onto latest `origin/main` before the final main merge if asked, to reduce conflicts.

